Myth: Long ago, Orea, the fiery guardian of the earth's molten heart, harbored a profound love for Aethel, the Weaver of the Heavens. While Aethel adorned the vast night with cold, unmoving stars, he longed for the fierce warmth of the world's hidden fires. Orea wished to share her realm's vibrant energy with him, but the silent, boundless void between the deep earth and the high sky kept them apart.

Determined to bridge the expanse, Orea journeyed into the deepest magma chambers, gathering thousands of radiant, undying embers. She carried these glowing sparks to the summit of the tallest caldera and unleashed a colossal eruption, launching the brilliant fires upward into the celestial twilight.

Zephyrus, the bitter wind spirit who despised their bond, unleashed a howling, icy tempest to extinguish the ascending flames. However, the fierce gales only fueled the embers, whipping them into a sweeping rain of blazing light across the dark night.

Aethel reached out, catching the swirling tide. With delicate fingers, he wove the fleeting fires into the cosmic canvas, letting them streak brilliantly through the dark. Today, this luminous spectacle is known as the meteor shower, an eternal testament to their unyielding love.
